=======================================================================

SCHOOL MANAGEMENT SYSTEM - PROJECT README

=======================================================================

1.  INTRODUCTION

The School Management System is a comprehensive administrative tool
designed to manage the student lifecycle, staff assignments, and
institutional infrastructure. Built with a focus on data integrity and
security, the application employs an Object-Oriented approach in
Python, backed by a MySQL relational database normalised to the 3rd
Normal Form (3NF).

=======================================================================

2. ARTEFACT CODEBASE REQUIREMENT SPECIFICATION COMPLETION

2.1. Required improvement to the codebase. (9/9)
R1. Added code comments to explain the code.
R2. Organized the code into different files/classes and folders;
Made sure my solution is a proper Object Oriented solution including:
Inheritance, Encapsulation, Abstraction, Single Responsibility.
R3. Implemented a well-designed database including necessary
constraints and 3NF tables.
R4. CRUD functionalities were fully implemented to manage students,
teachers, courses, teaching and registration records making the data be
easily manipulated.
R5. Used Merge Sort and Binary Search algorithms to filter and sort
loaded data. The program allows searching for specific records by IDs,
First or Last name, Date, Course.
R6. Errors and Exceptions were handled using try-except,
SIGNAL SQLSTATE...SET MESSAGE_TEXT...
R7. Implemented input validation on multiple layers of the program:
menus, models, stored procedures and tables level.
R8. Followed PEP8 Standards.
R9. Implemented loops providing a continuously running program until
the user's decision to quit.

2.2. Optional improvements to the codebase. (6/7)
O1. Implemented a login feature validating username and password
stored in Authentication table.
O2. Added more entities and tables: Authentication, Administration,
